  "slug": "assessment-atrial-electromechanical-0756",
  "summary": "Recent preprints pair subject-specific network analysis with multivariate comparison of individual brain network configurations.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is individualized brain network analysis, represented here by IndivSTATIS, a multivariate STATIS-based method that compares individualized parcellations and networks within a shared component space. The other two preprints do not address brain network modeling. One is a multiscale circulation model coupling systemic hemodynamics, cerebral autoregulation, and imaging-derived Circle of Willis networks to simulate flow under anatomical variations and stenosis. The other is a MICCAI 2024 challenge report on deep learning for enlarged perivascular space MRI segmentation, in which top methods degrade on an unseen cohort. What is new in IndivSTATIS is the explicit comparison of individual brain network configurations within a single shared component space.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2025-12-26"
}
